Fallback clips carry a status instead of having audio swapped in during tts: writing the original vocals slice as the clip would let fit trim its leading silence (shifting it off the speaker's mouth) and let mix loudness-match and duck it, so mix reads vocals.wav directly for fallback_original, at unity and unducked, and masks it out of keep_vocals to avoid doubling. The content-word check is a bag-of-words test (word >= 4 letters, not a substring of the joined transcript, no heard word with SequenceMatcher ratio >= 0.6) rather than an alignment backtrace: WER already covers order, and the substring rule keeps joined names (Manakumagai) and the ratio keeps near-spellings (Kumagae) passing, while strengths/drinks (~0.4) fails. Rephrase is tried only once per line because each try costs a full round of TTS seeds plus ASR. The fit regenerator now returns None on a failed check and restores the translation, since otherwise a shortened but misheard line would bypass the fallback entirely. 'auto' uses 1 s as the cutoff because short lines are mostly backchannels where the original voice is less jarring than a gap.
